  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "Beneath the southern edge of the Bermuda Triangle, the Atlantic seafloor plunges more than eight thousand meters into pitch-black abyss.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 6.516,
      "duration": 6.416,
      "pause_after": 0.4,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "eight",
        "thousand",
        "meters",
        "pitch-black",
        "abyss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "That chasm is the Puerto Rico Trench\u2014the deepest point in the entire Atlantic Ocean. Before modern sonar and deep-sea robots, any ship sinking over trenches this deep simply vanished beyond human reach\u2014turning tragic wrecks into legends.",
      "rate": "-5%",
      "pitch": "-2Hz",
      "start": 6.916,
      "end": 20.527,
      "duration": 13.611,
      "pause_after": 0.42,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "Puerto",
        "Rico",
        "Trench",
        "deepest",
        "vanished"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "Above the seafloor, powerful physics takes over. Where the fast, warm Gulf Stream slams into Atlantic storms, sudden thirty-meter rogue waves can overwhelm steel cargo ships in minutes\u2014like the SS Cotopaxi, lost in 1925 and finally identified underwater decades later.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 20.947,
      "end": 38.042,
      "duration": 17.096,
      "pause_after": 0.44,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "powerful",
        "physics",
        "thirty-meter",
        "rogue",
        "waves",
        "Cotopaxi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "Some once blamed giant seafloor methane eruptions for sinking ships. While dense gas plumes can reduce buoyancy in lab tanks, U.S. Geological Survey records show no massive hydrate blowouts have struck this region in fifteen thousand years.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-2Hz",
      "start": 38.482,
      "end": 52.472,
      "duration": 13.989,
      "pause_after": 0.46,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "methane",
        "eruptions",
        "no",
        "massive",
        "fifteen",
        "thousand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "Yet seismologists did uncover a real anomaly deeper underground.",
      "rate": "-4%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 52.932,
      "end": 56.762,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "pause_after": 0.44,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "real",
        "anomaly",
        "deeper",
        "underground"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "Directly beneath Bermuda's crust sits an unusual twenty-kilometer-thick layer of frozen mantle rock\u2014a hidden geological raft holding the surrounding seafloor five hundred meters higher than normal.",
      "rate": "+0%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 57.202,
      "end": 67.379,
      "duration": 10.177,
      "pause_after": 0.46,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "twenty-kilometer-thick",
        "geological",
        "raft",
        "five",
        "hundred"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "According to NOAA, ships don't disappear here more often than in any other stormy shipping lane. What hides beneath the Bermuda Triangle isn't folklore\u2014it's extreme ocean physics and an eight-kilometer abyss.",
      "rate": "-5%",
      "pitch": "-2Hz",
      "start": 67.839,
      "end": 80.027,
      "duration": 12.188,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": [
        "isn't",
        "folklore",
        "extreme",
        "physics",
        "eight-kilometer",
        "abyss"
      ]
    }
  ],
